  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2d1e83780892b5c4592add1c4998da52, type: 3}
  m_Name: TechnologyFacts
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FactPack
  category: 5
  facts:
  - The first computer bug was an actual moth.
  - More people have mobile phones than toilets.
  - The first electronic computer ENIAC weighed 27 tons.
  - Google was originally called Backrub.
  - Domain names were free until 1995.
  - Russia has more surface area than Pluto.
  - Over 3.5 billion people use the internet.
  - NASA's internet speed is 91 GB per second.
  - The first hard drive could only hold 5 MB of data.
  - CAPTCHA stands for 'Completely Automated Public Turing test to tell Computers
    and Humans Apart'.
  - Every minute, 500 hours of video are uploaded to YouTube.
  - The QWERTY keyboard was designed to slow down typing speed.
  - There are more than 1.5 billion active websites.
